# Docker build context -- an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list, so a new file in the
# working tree stays out of the image until someone decides it belongs there.
#
# The `*` below must stay the first line. It excludes the entire working tree;
# each `!` line under it re-includes exactly one path the image build reads.
# Move `*` down, or drop it, and every `!` line becomes decoration while the
# whole working tree is sent to the daemon -- including a real saneless config
# file with a live paperless-ngx token, which is then recoverable from the
# build cache and from the discarded builder stage.
#
# This is one of TWO independent gates. The other is the explicit `COPY` lines
# in the builder stage of the Dockerfile, which replaced `COPY . .`. A mistake
# in either one alone cannot leak a secret into a layer; both would have to be
# wrong at once.
#
# None of these is optional. The builder stage runs `uv sync --locked`, which
# fails outright without uv.lock. pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"` and the PEP 639 `license-files = ["LICENSE"]`, and the
# project build fails outright when either file is missing from the context.
#
# `!src/` re-includes the directory and everything beneath it; `!src/**` is not
# needed. Pinned by tests/test_deployment_config.py, because nothing else in CI
# would notice this list being weakened: the image still builds and runs with
# extra files in its context.
*
!src/
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
